+// |payload_len| the length of its payload. Zero for either keeps BoringSSL's
+// choice: AES-128-GCM with AES hardware, otherwise ChaCha20-Poly1305, and a
+// random length. It returns one on success and zero if |aead_id| is not a
+// supported HPKE AEAD.
+//
+// A client imitating another's ClientHello can use it to send the same ECH
+// GREASE.
+OPENSSL_EXPORT int SSL_set_ech_grease_shape(SSL *ssl, uint16_t aead_id,
+                                            size_t payload_len);
